WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.802
Hi! How are the two rails of a railway track different from two roads at a crossroads? Today we'll learn about parallel and perpendicular lines.

2
00:00:11.952 --> 00:00:19.650
Parallel lines are like railway tracks. They stay the same distance apart and never meet, however long they are.

3
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.546
On diagrams, small arrows often show that lines are parallel.

4
00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:30.162
Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle, like a crossroads or the letter T.

5
00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:35.346
A small square where they meet shows it's a right angle.

6
00:00:35.496 --> 00:00:43.530
In a rectangle, the top and bottom are parallel, and so are the left and right. That's 2 pairs of parallel sides.

7
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.194
Neighbouring sides of a rectangle are perpendicular, because they meet at right angles.

8
00:00:49.344 --> 00:00:55.626
In the letter H, the two upright lines are parallel, and the middle line is perpendicular to them.

9
00:00:55.776 --> 00:01:02.370
To check if two lines are perpendicular, use the right angle of a set square.

10
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:09.546
Watch out! Some pupils say two lines are parallel just because they don't touch. That's wrong!

11
00:01:09.696 --> 00:01:14.562
If the lines get closer and would meet when drawn longer, they're not parallel.

12
00:01:14.712 --> 00:01:19.938
Parallel lines are the same distance apart everywhere.

13
00:01:20.088 --> 00:01:29.250
Your turn! What kind of lines are the two rails of a railway track? Pause and think.

14
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:37.674
They stay the same distance apart and never meet. They're parallel lines. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:37.824 --> 00:01:46.314
Another one! What kind of lines make the letter T? Pause and think.

16
00:01:46.464 --> 00:01:53.706
They meet at a right angle. They're perpendicular lines. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:53.856 --> 00:02:03.162
Here's another! How many pairs of parallel sides does a square have? Pause and think.

18
00:02:03.312 --> 00:02:09.714
Top and bottom, left and right: 2 pairs. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:09.864 --> 00:02:18.810
Try one more! What angle do perpendicular lines make? Pause and think.

20
00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:25.170
Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:36.978
Last one! Neighbouring sides of a rectangle are perpendicular. How many right angles does it have? Pause and think.

22
00:02:37.128 --> 00:02:42.858
All 4 angles are right angles. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:43.008 --> 00:02:53.010
Remember: parallel lines are the same distance apart and never meet. Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle, and we can check with a set square.

24
00:02:53.160 --> 00:03:00.042
Look for parallel and perpendicular lines at home, like window frames and shelves!

